0..70 Comment "// A case arm learns its fields from the injectivity of a constructor."
71..73 Comment "//"
74..151 Comment "// The arm binds a path between two applications of one constructor. Its goal"
152..228 Comment "// reads the fields of one side, and its body gives the fields of the other."
229..231 Comment "//"
232..305 Comment "// The checker splits that path into one path for each field that the two"
306..383 Comment "// applications write apart. A later step solves each field path. The checker"
384..459 Comment "// does not split a constructor whose field types read an earlier field, as"
460..535 Comment "// the pathological twin shows. The vector and bound programs `tail`, `zip`"
536..581 Comment "// and `lookup` learn their lengths this way."
582..584 Comment "//"
585..600 Comment "// - see: #3403"
601..671 Comment "// - see: #3481 — the spike that wrote the vector and bound programs"
673..710 Comment "// The naturals the indices count in."
